  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisting the Government of Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under this project, International Organization for Migration (IOM) will partner with two local NGOs to support the government of Guineas efforts to combat trafficking in persons by reinforcing the capacities of the government body responsible for preventing human trafficking, protecting victims, and prosecuting perpetrators. IOM will provide training to police, border officials, labor inspectors, prosecutors, and magistrates, with a focus on the legislative framework as stipulated in the 2016 Guinean penal code. IOM will create a coordination mechanism among government, civil society, and private sector actors to support and strengthen awareness against false job offers and prevent young migrants from falling into trafficking networks. IOM will help develop, and train officials to implement, guidelines for NGOs and government counterparts on victim identification and provision of protection services. IOMs NGO partners will raise awareness on TIP in seven regions of the country and will administer reintegration grants for victims of trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
